Tests ability to design a practical string data structure and reason about trade-offs between block sizes, memory usage, and update costs. It combines data structure design with amortized analysis.

## Key Concepts
- **Sqrt-decomposition**: Partition data into blocks of size ~√n to achieve O(√n) per operation
- **Block splitting/merging**: Dynamic resizing maintains balance; split at 2B, merge below B/2
- **Per-block frequency counts**: Precomputed arrays enable O(1) lookups per block during range queries
- **Amortized analysis**: While individual operations may touch multiple blocks, the split/merge strategy ensures overall O(√n) amortized cost

